public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.F4.ShortRoot.Derivation

/-!
# The derivation equations of the type-F4 multiplication, entry by entry

The invariant symmetric multiplication of the twenty-six-dimensional module of type `F₄` has at
most two nonzero structure constants in each of three directions: for a fixed first factor and a
fixed second factor the product is supported on at most two basis vectors, for a fixed first
factor and a fixed target at most two second factors contribute, and for a fixed second factor and
a fixed target at most two first factors contribute. Each of the three follows from the additivity
of weights along a nonzero structure constant, together with the fact that every weight space of
the module has dimension at most two.

The first of the three is the column structure tabulated in
`TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.F4.ShortRoot.InvariantStructure`. This file tabulates the other two and draws
the consequence: the `(i, j)` entry of the derivation equation on the `k`th column is an identity
between two sums of two products, each a matrix entry times a table lookup.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.F4ShortRoot.multRowTargetOne` and its three companions: the row structure of a
  multiplication operator.
* `TauCeti.F4ShortRoot.multIndexOne` and its three companions: the structure of the multiplication
  operators as a family indexed by the first factor.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.F4ShortRoot.isDoubleStep_transpose_multiplicationOperator`: the transpose of a
  multiplication operator has at most two nonzero entries in each column.
* `TauCeti.F4ShortRoot.multiplicationBy_apply`: an entry of the operator of multiplication by a
  vector, as a two-term sum.
* `TauCeti.F4ShortRoot.IsDerivation.entry`: **the derivation equations entry by entry.**
-/

